fpm's [library.source-dir] takes one directory and its scanner does not
preprocess, so this directory exists to give it exactly the set that always
compiles:

    ln -s ../src         port
    ln -s ../include/libfint.f90            .
    ln -s ../include/libcint_interface.f90  .

f12/ and polyfit/ are deliberately not here.  The F12 sources are guarded by
COMPILE_F12 and would compile to nothing, but fpm reads `use` statements
lexically -- it cannot see a preprocessor conditional -- so a guarded
`use cint_tab_stg_roots` still reads to it as a dependency on a 100 MB table
that is not in this repository.  The polyfit tables need
-fmax-array-constructor, and fpm's --flag replaces the profile flags rather
than adding to them, which would silently drop -fcheck=bounds.

CMake compiles all of them; only fpm needs this.
